    "commit_message": "self-improvement-findings: heartbeat, fix /tmp data-loss risk, fix stale-sort bug\n\nCouncil follow-up (self-improvement-findings, 2026-08-29). Correction first:\ntold the council orchestrator.py had no scheduling and ran manually once -\nwrong, caused by a grep miss (self.improvement vs the real unit name\nself-improving-system). It's been running daily via\nself-improving-system.timer since 2026-08-23. Adjusted scope accordingly -\nno re-scheduling needed, just the 3 things below.\n\n- orchestrator.py: record_heartbeat() on every run (ok/failed), matching\n  the platform's standard job-health convention. This timer had zero\n  observability - if it silently stopped or errored, nothing would notice.\n\n- orchestrator.py --data-root default: /tmp/usstjros-findings ->\n  /opt/starship-endeavour/data/self-improvement. The timer had been\n  writing 6+ days of run history to a path with no persistence guarantee\n  across reboot, undetected. Migrated the existing /tmp history over\n  (data/self-improvement/runs/2026-08-23 through 2026-08-28) rather than\n  losing it.\n\n- dashboard.py DATA_ROOT: was \"prefer /tmp if it exists, else persistent\n  path\" - the /tmp-preference was its own separate bug (permanent silent\n  disagreement with a fixed orchestrator.py) independent of the read-only-\n  root rationale, which no longer holds on this host anyway (verified\n  writable). Now unconditionally the persistent path.\n\n- dashboard.py get_latest_run(): found while verifying the migration above.\n  Lexicographic sort on directory name broke the moment old\n  r_20260712_NNN-style dirs mixed with new date-prefixed ones ('r' > '2'\n  in ASCII), so a July run always outranked an August one as \"latest\" -\n  the dashboard would have shown 0 findings, worse than before this fix.\n  Switched to mtime-based sort.\n\nVerified: py_compile clean, dashboard.py restarted and /api/status\nconfirms latest_run=2026-08-28-210431, findings_count=2 (matches live API\nbefore any change). Nav link still open (separate commit).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F1KgvHcPTh7uQNNPDtxRuj",
